plan:
Based on this analysis, our potential plans going forward might include:
- Keeping the price above 13.0 as this increases profit significantly;
- Ensuring that we have a high quantity of stock in trading rounds to maximize profit based on the trend observed between round 67-73 where a balance between quantity and price per unit led to increased profit;
- Running promotions or advertising campaigns when the market demand is low, possibly by slightly lowering our prices to attract more customers and still make a profit.

3.

insight:
In light of the data:
- The optimal price point appears to be around 13.0;
- The highest sales didn't necessarily mean the highest profits due to the profit margin being impactful;
- High quantity sales were more profitable than low priced, high volume sales;
- Lowering the price slightly can increase customer acquisition while still earning a healthy profit.

